cBioPortal data
---------------
cbioportal-link queries the public cBioPortal web API (https://api.cbioportal.org) live and
stores no cBioPortal data. Unless a study states otherwise, data in cBioPortal are available
under the ODC Open Database License (ODbL 1.0,
https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1.0/) with attribution to the original studies.
Some studies set their own terms in their description (for example msk_chord_2024:
Creative Commons BY-NC-ND 4.0); each response row carries the study's licence, a
`restricted` flag, its citation and PMID, and restricted studies are excluded unless the
caller opts in.

Cite cBioPortal:
  Gao J et al. Integrative analysis of complex cancer genomics and clinical profiles using
  the cBioPortal. Sci Signal 2013. PMID 23550210.
  de Bruijn I et al. Analysis and visualization of longitudinal genomic and clinical data
  from the AACR Project GENIE Biopharma Collaborative in cBioPortal. Cancer Res 2023.
  PMID 37668528.
and each study's own publication.

Cancer Hotspots data (bundled)
------------------------------
cbioportal_link/data/hotspots_grch37.txt and hotspots_grch38.txt are derived from Cancer
Hotspots (https://www.cancerhotspots.org, https://www.3dhotspots.org), Memorial Sloan
Kettering Cancer Center. The data are licensed under the ODC Open Database License
(ODbL 1.0) as stated by cancerhotspots.org (cBioPortal/cancerhotspots commit b257eeaf).
The derived tables are offered under the same ODbL 1.0 licence. They were built by
scripts/build_hotspots.py from genome-nexus/genome-nexus-importer commit
4c2d0525d1f5686246ecb159cb8ad9c1962f28b4 (hotspots_v2_v3_and_3d.txt, sha256 recorded in
cbioportal_link/data/hotspots_provenance.json), keeping the v2 and 3D hotspots. No Cancer
Hotspots source code (AGPL-3.0) is included.

Cite Cancer Hotspots:
  Chang MT et al. Identifying recurrent mutations in cancer reveals widespread lineage
  diversity and mutational specificity. Nat Biotechnol 2016. PMID 26619011.
  Chang MT et al. Accelerating discovery of functional mutant alleles in cancer.
  Cancer Discov 2018. PMID 29247016.
  Gao J et al. 3D clusters of somatic mutations in cancer reveal numerous rare mutations as
  functional targets. Genome Med 2017. PMID 28115009.
